    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0324" n="1058" xml:id="pg1058"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Peirce.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Breckinridge’s No. 71,
                    of the 17th ultimo, inclosing copy of his note to the Russian foreign office in
                    regard to the refusal of the Russian consul-general at New York to visé
                    passports for American citizens of Jewish faith.</p>
                <p>His note is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
